-The milk study used HPLC to analyze individual ginsenosides and a trained panel for descriptive sensory analysis, including flavored and unflavored milks. Its abstract reports that adding vanilla flavor and sucralose reduced bitterness attributable to the extract.[1] The opposite blanket claim—that heat-associated bitterness simply has to be accepted—is therefore also too strong: a sensory improvement was observed in this particular formulation.[1]
